// `shrink-0` and `truncate` on one element cancel each other out.
//
// `truncate` is `overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space:
// nowrap`. None of it does anything until the element is narrower than its own
// content, and `flex-shrink: 0` is the rule that says it never will be. The
// pair reads as "cut this if it runs long" and behaves as "let this push
// everything else out of the row".
//
// Two shipped that way. A source declaring forty languages took the whole
// source row and left the name — `flex-1 truncate` — no width at all, which on
// screen was rows overlapping with their titles gone. The queue's series title
// carried the same pair, waiting for a long enough title.
//
// The fix is `shrink` with `min-w-0`, plus a `max-w-*` when the element should
// not take its share of the row to begin with.
//
// The pattern is a regex over the class string rather than a JSX-shaped
// pattern: Biome's GritQL does not match `className=$c`, and bare `$class`
// matches every node in the file. The regex is anchored, so it matches the
// string literal itself and not the elements containing it. Covers `"…"` and
// `` `…` ``; a class assembled by a helper call is out of reach.
//
// Verified to fire on both orders and on a template literal, and not on
// `shrink truncate`, `shrink-0 rounded-full`, or either class alone.
language js

$class where {
  or {
    $class <: r"[\"`][^\"`]*shrink-0[^\"`]*truncate[^\"`]*[\"`]",
    $class <: r"[\"`][^\"`]*truncate[^\"`]*shrink-0[^\"`]*[\"`]"
  },
  register_diagnostic(span=$class, message="`shrink-0` with `truncate`: a flex child that cannot shrink is never narrower than its content, so `truncate` never engages and the element pushes its siblings out of the row instead. Use `min-w-0 shrink truncate`, with a `max-w-*` if it should not take the whole row.", severity="error")
}
